prompt:
You are a legal analyst preparing an evaluation reference for business process models. Read the process description and ONE passage of EU law, and state whether the passage creates obligations for this specific process, and if so, which process steps it requires.

INSTRUCTIONS
- First decide whether the passage concerns this kind of process at all (same kind of parties, transaction, contract, payment, delivery or communication). If not, the label is "irrelevant".
- If it does, list the facts the rule depends on (for example who the parties are, how the contract is concluded, what triggers the rule, any exception). Judge each fact using only what the description says.
- Label:
  - "applicable": the description states every fact the rule depends on.
  - "not_applicable": the description states at least one fact that excludes the rule.
  - "indeterminate": the rule concerns this process, but the description does not state enough facts to decide.
  Do not assume facts that are not written. A "customer" is not necessarily a "consumer"; it may be a business.
- required_steps: ONLY for "applicable". Each step is an activity that the process must contain to comply, written as a short BPMN task label in the form verb + object (for example "Provide withdrawal information"), with who performs it and, if the rule says so, when (before or after which existing step of the description). Only steps that the passage itself requires; nothing from other laws or general good practice. If the rule is already fully met by steps the description contains, list those steps anyway and set already_in_description to true.
- possible_steps: ONLY for "indeterminate". The steps the passage WOULD require if it applied, in the same format.
- evidence: copy the parts of the process description that support your judgement, word for word.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "Fact": {
      "properties": {
        "fact": {
          "description": "A fact the rule depends on, short",
          "title": "Fact",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
          "enum": [
            "stated_true",
            "stated_false",
            "not_stated"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "fact",
        "status"
      ],
      "title": "Fact",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Step": {
      "properties": {
        "label": {
          "description": "Short BPMN task label, verb + object, e.g. 'Provide withdrawal information'",
          "title": "Label",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "actor": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "Who performs it, or null",
          "title": "Actor"
        },
        "timing": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "description": "When, relative to the existing steps, if the rule says so; or null",
          "title": "Timing"
        },
        "already_in_description": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "true if the description already contains this step",
          "title": "Already In Description",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "label"
      ],
      "title": "Step",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "label": {
      "enum": [
        "applicable",
        "not_applicable",
        "indeterminate",
        "irrelevant"
      ],
      "title": "Label",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "facts": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Fact"
      },
      "title": "Facts",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "reason": {
      "description": "One or two sentences",
      "title": "Reason",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "required_steps": {
      "description": "Only for applicable",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Step"
      },
      "title": "Required Steps",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "possible_steps": {
      "description": "Only for indeterminate",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Step"
      },
      "title": "Possible Steps",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "evidence": {
      "description": "Exact quotes from the description",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "title": "Evidence",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "label",
    "reason"
  ],
  "title": "SilverOutput",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
This process begins when a potential customer inquires about a product or service.
Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions.
If the customer is interested, they are guided through selecting the appropriate product or service.
Next, the sales representative provides a quote, and after approval from the customer, the process moves to order placement.
The order is then recorded in the system, and the customer receives confirmation of their order.
The process ends when the order is successfully placed and confirmed.

LEGAL PASSAGE
[GDPR-Art13-3] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
3. Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected, the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2.

raw_output:
{
  "label": "indeterminate",
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact": "Personal data are collected from the data subject",
      "status": "stated_true"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which they were collected",
      "status": "not_stated"
    }
  ],
  "reason": "The process involves collection of personal data, so Article 13‑3 is relevant, but the description does not state whether the controller will later use the data for a different purpose.",
  "possible_steps": [
    {
      "label": "Provide further processing information",
      "actor": "controller",
      "timing": "before further processing",
      "already_in_description": false
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    "This process begins when a potential customer inquires about a product or service.",
    "Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions."
  ]
}

